userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the backward-compatible PROJECT thread kind and explicit runner capability contract without changing protocol version.

**Motivation** — The koda assistant (S5b) must answer questions such as "which tickets are blocked?" that have nothing to do with a repo checkout.

**Approach** — Protocol package (`packages/fleet-protocol/src/threads.ts`, `index.ts`; US-001, additive only)

- `ChatThreadKind` — new: `export type ChatThreadKind = 'REPO' | 'PROJECT'` and `export const CHAT_THREAD_KINDS = ['REPO', 'PROJECT'] as const`, re-exported from `index.ts`.
- `ThreadAssign` — Target: gains `kind?: ChatThreadKind` (documented: absent means `REPO`). `feature` stays `string`.
- `RunnerCapabilities` (`index.ts:64-81`) — Target: gains `projectThreads?: true` ("Fleet S5b: the runner hosts PROJECT threads with no checkout. Absent on older runners.").

API contract (US-001)

- `apps/api/src/fleet/common/thread-jobs.ts` — re-exports `ChatThreadKind` and mirrors `CHAT_THREAD_KINDS` at runtime, as it does `THREAD_COMMAND_TYPES`.
- `parseCapabilitiesCore` (`apps/api/src/fleet/common/capabilities-core.ts:118-158`) — Target: accepts `projectThreads`, strict like `threadWrite` (only exactly `true`; any other present value fails with reason `projectThreads`); the parsed result has `projectThreads: true` only when the report had it.
- `RunnerSummaryDto` (`apps/api/src/fleet/runners/dto/runner-summary.dto.ts`) — Target: gains `projectThreads: boolean`, true iff `protocolVersion >= THREAD_MIN_PROTOCOL_VERSION` and the stored capabilities have `projectThreads === true`.

S5b-R9: no protocol version bump. The ASSIGN `thread` block gains an optional `kind`; a runner advertises `projectThreads: true`; PROJECT THREAD jobs are placed only on runners that advertise it.

1a-R1: the API always sends `thread.kind` (`REPO` or `PROJECT`) on a THREAD ASSIGN. A runner treats a missing `kind` as `REPO`. `ThreadAssign.feature` stays a required string: for a PROJECT thread the API sends `thread-<threadId>` (the job's own feature), and the runner never uses it for a PROJECT run. This keeps the runner's existing `feature: string` consumers (`thread-worktree.ts`, `thread-publish.ts`, `thread-action-run.ts`) unchanged.

1a-R6: the new protocol type is named `ChatThreadKind` (not `ThreadKind`), because `isThreadKind(command)` already means "the job command is THREAD".

Update existing exact expectations: runner-summary.dto.spec.ts capability-free result gains projectThreads: false; fleet-openapi.contract.spec.ts and test/integration/fleet/runner-views.integration.spec.ts sorted summary keys gain projectThreads. Other expectations unchanged. Regenerate openapi.json via bun run api:export-spec and refresh the generated CLI via bun run generate; never manually edit generated clients. The API runtime mirror must not introduce a production runtime import from the workspace protocol package; the parity unit test uses a runtime import.

**Scope** — In: shared additive wire types/constants, API capability parsing, project runner summary and related contract regeneration/tests. Out: schema/guards (US-002), creation (US-003), session jobs (US-004), ASSIGN/placement integration (US-005), runner execution (US-006), web scope picker (US-007); no protocol bump or kodaTools capability.

**Interface** —
```ts
export type ChatThreadKind = 'REPO' | 'PROJECT';
export const CHAT_THREAD_KINDS = ['REPO', 'PROJECT'] as const;
// ThreadAssign gains:
kind?: ChatThreadKind;
// RunnerCapabilities gains:
projectThreads?: true;
// RunnerSummaryDto gains:
projectThreads: boolean;
```
